      "problem": "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{3{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}-2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "For any non-constant polynomial $P(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\pm \\infty }(\\frac{1}{P(x)})=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $3{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}-2$ is a non-constant polynomial, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{3{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}-2}=0.\n$$",
